<article class="env-lemma" id="05S0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05S0">Lemma <span data-tag="05S0">13.13.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The functor $K(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})) \longrightarrow \text{Gr}(\mathcal{A})$, $K^\bullet \longmapsto H^0(\text{gr}(K^\bullet ))$ is homological. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The functor $K(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})) \rightarrow \mathcal{A}$, $K^\bullet \longmapsto H^0(\text{gr}^ p(K^\bullet ))$ is homological. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The functor $K(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})) \longrightarrow \mathcal{A}$, $K^\bullet \longmapsto H^0((\text{forget }F)K^\bullet )$ is homological. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the fact that $H^0 : K(\mathcal{A}) \to \mathcal{A}$ is homological, see Lemma <a href="/tag/05RS" data-tag="05RS">13.11.1</a> and the fact that the functors $\text{gr}, \text{gr}^ p, (\text{forget }F)$ are exact functors of triangulated categories. See Lemma <a href="/tag/05QZ" data-tag="05QZ">13.4.20</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>